  },
  "segment_count": 65,
  "segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "start": 7.59,
      "end": 9.61,
      "duration": 2.02,
      "text": "PROFESSOR: Hello, and welcome to a help session on"
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "start": 9.61,
      "end": 10.91,
      "duration": 1.3,
      "text": "complementation."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "start": 10.91,
      "end": 12.3,
      "duration": 1.39,
      "text": "Today, we are going to be working"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "start": 12.3,
      "end": 14.12,
      "duration": 1.82,
      "text": "out a problem together."
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "start": 14.12,
      "end": 16.6,
      "duration": 2.48,
      "text": "If you have not yet had a chance to work out the problem"
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "start": 16.6,
      "end": 20.37,
      "duration": 3.77,
      "text": "on your own, please do so now, and then return to this video."
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "start": 31.54,
      "end": 33.79,
      "duration": 2.25,
      "text": "All right, now that you've had a chance to look at the"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "start": 33.79,
      "end": 36.85,
      "duration": 3.06,
      "text": "problem your on, let's work it out together."
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "start": 36.85,
      "end": 40.82,
      "duration": 3.97,
      "text": "So, here we have a series of different fruit flies."
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "start": 40.82,
      "end": 44.9,
      "duration": 4.08,
      "text": "They all have these recessive mini-fly phenotypes."
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "start": 44.9,
      "end": 46.46,
      "duration": 1.56,
      "text": "So, we've noticed that there are lots"
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "start": 46.46,
      "end": 48.14,
      "duration": 1.68,
      "text": "of different mutations."
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "start": 48.14,
      "end": 49.87,
      "duration": 1.73,
      "text": "And, now, we would like to put them into"
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "start": 49.87,
      "end": 51.93,
      "duration": 2.06,
      "text": "complementation groups."
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "start": 51.93,
      "end": 55.99,
      "duration": 4.06,
      "text": "So, we start off by looking at this nice, large Punnett"
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "start": 55.99,
      "end": 58.62,
      "duration": 2.63,
      "text": "square we have, where all the flies have been crossed to"
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "start": 58.62,
      "end": 60.2,
      "duration": 1.58,
      "text": "each other."
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "start": 60.2,
      "end": 64.69,
      "duration": 4.49,
      "text": "So, if we look at A and B for instance, when these two flies"
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "start": 64.69,
      "end": 66.41,
      "duration": 1.72,
      "text": "are crossed together, they still"
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "start": 66.41,
      "end": 68.67,
      "duration": 2.26,
      "text": "have a mini-fly phenotype."
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "start": 68.67,
      "end": 73.45,
      "duration": 4.78,
      "text": "This means that the mutation is in the same gene and that"
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "start": 73.45,
      "end": 78.3,
      "duration": 4.85,
      "text": "these two mutants do not complement each other, but"
    },
    {
      "index": 22,
      "start": 78.3,
      "end": 80.95,
      "duration": 2.65,
      "text": "they make up one complementation group."
    },
    {
      "index": 23,
      "start": 80.95,
      "end": 85.63,
      "duration": 4.68,
      "text": "So if we look farther down this column, A and F together"
    },
    {
      "index": 24,
      "start": 85.63,
      "end": 88.98,
      "duration": 3.35,
      "text": "also have a mini-fly phenotype."
    },
    {
      "index": 25,
      "start": 88.98,
      "end": 94.73,
      "duration": 5.75,
      "text": "This means A, B, and F, all three of these are in the same"
    },
    {
      "index": 26,
      "start": 94.73,
      "end": 95.98,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "complementation group."
    },
    {
      "index": 27,
      "start": 104.02,
      "end": 107.24,
      "duration": 3.22,
      "text": "So, now that we've already looked at A and B, let's"
    },
    {
      "index": 28,
      "start": 107.24,
      "end": 113.8,
      "duration": 6.56,
      "text": "continue on to C. So, C has a normal fly in all of these"
    },
    {
      "index": 29,
      "start": 113.8,
      "end": 115.71,
      "duration": 1.91,
      "text": "instances except this one."
    },
    {
      "index": 30,
      "start": 115.71,
      "end": 120.57,
      "duration": 4.86,
      "text": "When C and E are crossed together, they also have a"
    },
    {
      "index": 31,
      "start": 120.57,
      "end": 122.43,
      "duration": 1.86,
      "text": "mini-fly phenotype."
    },
    {
      "index": 32,
      "start": 122.43,
      "end": 125.92,
      "duration": 3.49,
      "text": "Thus, C and E also form a complementation group."
    },
    {
      "index": 33,
      "start": 132.07,
      "end": 137.946,
      "duration": 5.876,
      "text": "So, now we're done with A,B, C, E, and F. So looking at D,"
    },
    {
      "index": 34,
      "start": 137.946,
      "end": 141.6,
      "duration": 3.654,
      "text": "D when crossed to all the other flies, you never get a"
    },
    {
      "index": 35,
      "start": 141.6,
      "end": 142.87,
      "duration": 1.27,
      "text": "mini-fly phenotype."
    },
    {
      "index": 36,
      "start": 142.87,
      "end": 146.76,
      "duration": 3.89,
      "text": "So, D must be in its own complementation group."
    },
    {
      "index": 37,
      "start": 151.5,
      "end": 155.73,
      "duration": 4.23,
      "text": "Great, so we've identified all three complementation groups."
    },
    {
      "index": 38,
      "start": 155.73,
      "end": 159.91,
      "duration": 4.18,
      "text": "So, moving on to the next part of the problem."
    },
    {
      "index": 39,
      "start": 159.91,
      "end": 165.65,
      "duration": 5.74,
      "text": "We are asked, are mutations B and C in the same gene, or are"
    },
    {
      "index": 40,
      "start": 165.65,
      "end": 168.21,
      "duration": 2.56,
      "text": "they in different genes?"
    },
    {
      "index": 41,
      "start": 168.21,
      "end": 175.21,
      "duration": 7.0,
      "text": "All right, so, if we look over here at B and C together, when"
    },
    {
      "index": 42,
      "start": 175.21,
      "end": 178.74,
      "duration": 3.53,
      "text": "these are crossed, we get a normal fly."
    },
    {
      "index": 43,
      "start": 178.74,
      "end": 181.57,
      "duration": 2.83,
      "text": "This means that the mutations were able to"
    },
    {
      "index": 44,
      "start": 181.57,
      "end": 183.43,
      "duration": 1.86,
      "text": "complement each other."
    },
    {
      "index": 45,
      "start": 183.43,
      "end": 187.13,
      "duration": 3.7,
      "text": "Meaning that the two mutations occur in different genes, and,"
    },
    {
      "index": 46,
      "start": 187.13,
      "end": 189.5,
      "duration": 2.37,
      "text": "thus, when you cross the flies, they're able to"
    },
    {
      "index": 47,
      "start": 189.5,
      "end": 192.59,
      "duration": 3.09,
      "text": "compensate for each other."
    },
    {
      "index": 48,
      "start": 192.59,
      "end": 194.395,
      "duration": 1.805,
      "text": "So, they're in different genes."
    },
    {
      "index": 49,
      "start": 196.98,
      "end": 199.59,
      "duration": 2.61,
      "text": "All right, now, in the last part of the problem, we're"
    },
    {
      "index": 50,
      "start": 199.59,
      "end": 204.26,
      "duration": 4.67,
      "text": "told that we are introduced to a new fly, or a new mutant"
    },
    {
      "index": 51,
      "start": 204.26,
      "end": 209.69,
      "duration": 5.43,
      "text": "fly, G. When G is crossed to A, we get a"
    },
    {
      "index": 52,
      "start": 209.69,
      "end": 211.93,
      "duration": 2.24,
      "text": "mini-fly phenotype out."
    },
    {
      "index": 53,
      "start": 211.93,
      "end": 218.9,
      "duration": 6.97,
      "text": "Also, when we cross G to B, we also get a mini-fly phenotype."
    },
    {
      "index": 54,
      "start": 218.9,
      "end": 222.3,
      "duration": 3.4,
      "text": "So the question is, what does this suggest to us"
    },
    {
      "index": 55,
      "start": 222.3,
      "end": 225.48,
      "duration": 3.18,
      "text": "about mutant G?"
    },
    {
      "index": 56,
      "start": 225.48,
      "end": 230.47,
      "duration": 4.99,
      "text": "Looking over here, we notice that A and B are in the same"
    },
    {
      "index": 57,
      "start": 230.47,
      "end": 231.89,
      "duration": 1.42,
      "text": "complementation group."
    },
    {
      "index": 58,
      "start": 231.89,
      "end": 235.72,
      "duration": 3.83,
      "text": "When A and B are crossed together, we also get"
    },
    {
      "index": 59,
      "start": 235.72,
      "end": 240.69,
      "duration": 4.97,
      "text": "mini-flies So, this suggests to us that G is yet another"
    },
    {
      "index": 60,
      "start": 240.69,
      "end": 243.15,
      "duration": 2.46,
      "text": "member of this complementation group."
    },
    {
      "index": 61,
      "start": 259.92,
      "end": 263.51,
      "duration": 3.59,
      "text": "Thus, G also falls into complementation"
    },
    {
      "index": 62,
      "start": 263.51,
      "end": 266.28,
      "duration": 2.77,
      "text": "group number one."
    },
    {
      "index": 63,
      "start": 266.28,
      "end": 270.46,
      "duration": 4.18,
      "text": "This concludes our help problem on complementation."
    },
    {
      "index": 64,
      "start": 270.46,
      "end": 271.71,
      "duration": 1.25,
      "text": "Thank you for joining us."
    }
  ],
